{"nodes": [{"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_shallow_vs_deep_copy_what_shallow_means_shallow_copy", "label": "Shallow copy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/shallow-vs-deep-copy/what-shallow-means.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Top-level properties become independent; nested objects stay shared. Spread, Object.assign, slice, Array.from, concat are all shallow. [...users] is a new array of the same user objects."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_shallow_vs_deep_copy_what_shallow_means_deep_copy", "label": "Deep copy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/shallow-vs-deep-copy/what-shallow-means.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Duplicates the whole graph so nothing is shared. Reach for it only for snapshots, defensive copies of input you will mutate, or data handed to untrusted code."}, {"id": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_shallow_vs_deep_copy_what_shallow_means_path_copy", "label": "Copy the path, share the rest", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "build-css-p2/docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/shallow-vs-deep-copy/what-shallow-means.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Idiomatic React/Redux updates copy only changed levels. Shared identity makes prev===next a valid change check and is what React.memo needs. Deep-cloning state defeats memoisation."}], "edges": [{"source": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_shallow_vs_deep_copy_what_shallow_means_path_copy", "target": "build_css_p2_docs_javascript_pages_phase